  "facts": [
    "The Ted Williams Tunnel, opened in 1995, was Boston’s first major Big Dig link, built from twelve binocular steel sections fabricated in Baltimore and floated into place before being lowered into a dredged channel.",
    "At 90 feet below harbor surface, the tunnel’s underwater stretch is North America’s deepest under‑water highway connection, spanning 3,960 feet of submerged roadway.",
    "In 2003, the tunnel finally opened to all traffic, replacing its initial commercial‑only status and adding an E‑ZPass toll of $1.75 for Massachusetts users, with discounted rates for East Boston residents."
